# Append-only memory logs: two branches each adding an entry must merge without
# a conflict. `union` keeps both sides' insertions.
#
# Two consequences, documented in memory/c_memory_protocol.md:
#   1. Entries must be self-contained blocks — relative order after a union
#      merge is arbitrary.
#   2. Union merge is not conflict detection. If two branches edit the SAME
#      entry you silently get both. Never rewrite an entry; supersede it.
memory/dec_log.md       merge=union
memory/r_pr_history.md  merge=union
